  "conclusion": "No measurable CPU difference in any case (medians within run-to-run spread). Case 3 minus case 4 attributes ~11 us of native CPU to each Script source-function call, so removing one small nursery allocation per call is below the noise floor; the dominant per-call cost lies elsewhere in the dynamic call path and is handed to cluster P. The change removes per-call heap allocation and GC pressure with identical caller semantics."
